Z||000000||JohnnyK||10-05-2000||03:59 PM||||Well, after total dismantilation (thats a word, right?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I have found one or two things. The throw out bearing doesn't slide "too" smoothly on the shaft, but thats not the problem (According to my shop teacher, it's fine).. BUT, it does look like the tranny "arm/shaft" (That the slave pushes and it disengages the clutch) seems to have slipped on the rod it is attached to, so that when thrown, the arm bangs into the bell housing. Also, would you guys suggest that I replace my clutch? (It's got a little more to go, but I am going to sell this car. Would my price be able to go up a bit with a new clutch?) Thanks!||||reg||1
